{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352226116,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7ba1f1c001O2C48dNjhvwrV2","messageID":"msg_1c7ba121a001eXvw8rH0kfFhUG","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"text","text":"<think>The venv creation in /tmp/opencode got denied (the workdir param probably). Let me retry with the venv inside the workspace? The workspace is writable. But creating a venv inside the workspace might pollute the repo — .dockerignore excludes .venv. I'll create it at /workspace/.venv and it's gitignored via .dockerignore (but not .gitignore). Let me check .gitignore.\n\nActually, the deny rule was for external_directory action — the bash tool with workdir /tmp/opencode might have triggered it? It said \"external_directory\": deny * except /tmp/opencode/*... Hmm, /tmp/opencode should be allowed. Maybe the issue is `python3 -m venv venv` creating something? Let me just retry with a different approach: install to a venv in /workspace/.venv.\n\nLet me check .gitignore first.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794352226076,"end":1794352226109}}}
