{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352522733,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7bea5d9001wVi2e0BxvqnlPJ","messageID":"msg_1c7be96810010JA9lqFwC3hKEC","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"text","text":"<think>Everything works. Now, let me verify the frontend renders properly. Without a browser, I can at least check the built HTML/JS loads and use a DOM check. Maybe I can install a headless browser? The sandbox has npm registry access; `npx playwright install chromium` requires downloading the browser binary from a CDN (playwright.azureedge.net) which may not be accessible. Let me test quickly whether puppeteer/playwright can be installed and if the browser download works. It's worth a try for UI verification.\n\nActually, let me first check if there's any chromium in the image... Already checked — none.\n\nLet me try `npx playwright@latest install --dry-run`? Better: try installing playwright-core + downloading chromium. Let me attempt with a timeout, since network access beyond package registries is blocked (\"no other network access\"). So browser downloads will likely fail. Let me try quickly (30s timeout).\n\nAlternatively, I can do a lightweight render test with jsdom (npm package) to at least verify React mounts without errors. jsdom is available on npm. But the app calls fetch and localStorage; jsdom provides localStorage and we can stub fetch. That's a decent smoke test for runtime errors (e.g., a crash on mount). Let me do that: install jsdom as a dev dependency temporarily (not in package.json — use npx? `npm i --no-save jsdom`).\n\nActually, let me try the playwright chromium download first since a real browser test would be much morevaluable.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794352522713,"end":1794352522729}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794352530837,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c7bea31c75c39ea4d2b3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/frontend && timeout 90 npx --yes playwright@1.49.1 install chromium 2>&1 | tail -5"},"output":"Error: Failed to download Chromium 131.0.6778.33 (playwright build v1148), caused by\nError: Download failure, code=1\n    at ChildProcess.<anonymous> (/tmp/llmlab-deps/npm/_npx/f0a362733743bae2/node_modules/playwright-core/lib/server/registry/browserFetcher.js:91:16)\n    at ChildProcess.emit (node:events:514:28)\n    at ChildProcess._handle.onexit (node:internal/child_process:324:12)\n","metadata":{"output":"Error: Failed to download Chromium 131.0.6778.33 (playwright build v1148), caused by\nError: Download failure, code=1\n    at ChildProcess.<anonymous> (/tmp/llmlab-deps/npm/_npx/f0a362733743bae2/node_modules/playwright-core/lib/server/registry/browserFetcher.js:91:16)\n    at ChildProcess.emit (node:events:514:28)\n    at ChildProcess._handle.onexit (node:internal/child_process:324:12)\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/frontend && timeout 90 npx --yes playwright@1.49.1 install chromium 2>&1 | tail -5","time":{"start":1794352522721,"end":1794352530815}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7bea5dc001fmtNXKYHOglIr0","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","messageID":"msg_1c7be96810010JA9lqFwC3hKEC"}}
