{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352622542,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7c02bbd001Y4uFYZ0Jex6UOq","messageID":"msg_1c7c01c8a0013PHWX6xNaltVDs","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"text","text":"<think>The app renders. But \"Could not reach the server\" — my fetch stub has an issue: `global.fetch = (input, init) => {...}` uses the global `fetch` inside itself → infinite recursion? No — I assigned global.fetch to the arrow function which references `fetch` → resolves to global.fetch → recursion! Actually inside the arrow function, `fetch(...)` refers to the global binding `fetch`, which is now my arrow function → infinite recursion → \"Could not reach the server\" comes from the catch in api.ts (the recursion throws RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded).\n\nLet me fix the stub to use the original node fetch captured before overriding.\n\nAlso note the month grid rendered 42 cells (26...31 then 1..31 then 1..0?) — the text shows \"262728293031123456789101112131415161718192021222324252627282930123456\" which is 42 numbers. Good.\n\nLet me fix the fetch stub.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794352622525,"end":1794352622539}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794352622567,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c7c0273973a1a137388b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs","newString":"const nodeFetch = globalThis.fetch;\nglobal.fetch = (input, init) => {\n  const url = new URL(typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.url, \"http://localhost:8000\");\n  return nodeFetch(`http://127.0.0.1:8000${url.pathname}${url.search}`, init);\n};","oldString":"global.fetch = (input, init) => {\n  const url = new URL(typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.url, \"http://localhost:8000\");\n  return fetch(`http://127.0.0.1:8000${url.pathname}${url.search}`, init);\n};"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs\n+++ /workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs\n@@ -38,11 +38,12 @@\n global.DOMException = dom.window.DOMException;\n global.IntersectionObserver = dom.window.IntersectionObserver ?? class {};\n global.ResizeObserver = dom.window.ResizeObserver ?? class {};\n global.localStorage = dom.window.localStorage;\n+const nodeFetch = globalThis.fetch;\n global.fetch = (input, init) => {\n   const url = new URL(typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.url, \"http://localhost:8000\");\n-  return fetch(`http://127.0.0.1:8000${url.pathname}${url.search}`, init);\n+  return nodeFetch(`http://127.0.0.1:8000${url.pathname}${url.search}`, init);\n };\n \n const errors = [];\n dom.window.addEventListener(\"error\", (event) => errors.push(String(event.error || event.message)));\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs","patch":"Index: /workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs\n+++ /workspace/tmpjsdom/render.mjs\n@@ -38,11 +38,12 @@\n global.DOMException = dom.window.DOMException;\n global.IntersectionObserver = dom.window.IntersectionObserver ?? class {};\n global.ResizeObserver = dom.window.ResizeObserver ?? class {};\n global.localStorage = dom.window.localStorage;\n+const nodeFetch = globalThis.fetch;\n global.fetch = (input, init) => {\n   const url = new URL(typeof input === \"string\" ? input : input.url, \"http://localhost:8000\");\n-  return fetch(`http://127.0.0.1:8000${url.pathname}${url.search}`, init);\n+  return nodeFetch(`http://127.0.0.1:8000${url.pathname}${url.search}`, init);\n };\n \n const errors = [];\n dom.window.addEventListener(\"error\", (event) => errors.push(String(event.error || event.message)));\n","additions":2,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"tmpjsdom/render.mjs","time":{"start":1794352622534,"end":1794352622548}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7c02bc0001adZyF7a8ZUbEdY","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","messageID":"msg_1c7c01c8a0013PHWX6xNaltVDs"}}
