{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352662699,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7c0c89e001Gs6w3Zdr66EvOc","messageID":"msg_1c7c096fb001KgO6XxNGMUw9xj","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"text","text":"<think>Good progress. Issues:\n\n1. `scrollIntoView` is not implemented in jsdom → error in the header \"Sign in\"/\"Register\" buttons (and openCreateForm when not signed in). In real browsers it works, but let me guard it anyway: `element?.scrollIntoView?.({behavior:\"smooth\"})`. That's more robust.\n\n2. \"event deleted\" FAIL — after deleting, the text still includes \"Design review v2\". Why? Possibly because the event list still shows it, or because the details modal/notice contains the title (the notice says “Design review v2” was deleted!). Yes — the notice includes the title. My check is too strict. Let me check that the event chip is gone instead: check that no button contains \"Design review v2\" other than... the notice is a div, not a button. Let me refine the check to look for the absence of the chip button.\n\n3. \"day view rendered\" FAIL — my check was `doc.body.textContent.includes(\"events in this period\")` — the text is \"event in this period\" (singular) when there's 1 event! Since after deleting there might be 0 events → \"0 events in this period\" (plural, since 0 !== 1). Hmm, the check failed... Let me look: after deletion, the count text would be \"0 events in this period\" → contains \"events in this period\" → should pass. Unless the day view didn't render... Wait, the check for the day view also required clicking \"Day\". Hmm, but the failure might be because the delete failed and the notice shows. Let me debug more carefully after fixing the scrollIntoView guard and the delete check.\n\nActually — maybe the delete DID fail: the ConfirmDialog's \"Delete event\" button text is \"Delete event\", and `byText(\"button\", \"Delete event\")` might have matched the modal's delete button... Also, the ConfirmDialog's delete might have failed because the api.deleteEvent returned... let me check the server logs. Let me debug interactively.\n\n4. \"today button works\" FAIL — same \"events in this period\" check issue.\n\nLet me fix the scrollIntoView guard first, rebuild, and re-run with more debug output.\n\nAlso note: the delete confirmation test clicked \"Delete\" in the details modal — `byText(\"button\", \"Delete\")` matches exactly \"Delete\" → the details modal button. Good. Then \"Delete event\" → the confirm dialog button. But the details modal was still open behind the confirm dialog... After deleting, both should close.\n\nWait, there's a bug: in `handleDeleted` I use `deleting?.title` — but `setDeleting(null)` happens before... no: `const title = deleting?.title ?? \"Event\";` is computed first, then setDeleting(null). Fine.\n\nLet me check the server side: did the DELETE happen? Let me query the API for events.\n\nLet me also print the DOM text after the delete step fordebugging.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794352662686,"end":1794352662696}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794352662723,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_01a1c7c0c3ee708ebfb5fc59","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx","newString":"  const scrollToAuth = () => {\n    document.getElementById(\"auth-panel\")?.scrollIntoView?.({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n  };\n\n  const openCreateForm = (day: Date, minutes?: number) => {\n    if (!session) {\n      setAuthTab(\"login\");\n      scrollToAuth();\n      return;\n    }","oldString":"  const openCreateForm = (day: Date, minutes?: number) => {\n    if (!session) {\n      setAuthTab(\"login\");\n      document.getElementById(\"auth-panel\")?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n      return;\n    }"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -167,12 +167,16 @@\n   setAnchor(startOfDay(day));\n   setView(\"day\");\n };\n \n+const scrollToAuth = () => {\n+  document.getElementById(\"auth-panel\")?.scrollIntoView?.({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n+};\n+\n const openCreateForm = (day: Date, minutes?: number) => {\n   if (!session) {\n     setAuthTab(\"login\");\n-    document.getElementById(\"auth-panel\")?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n+    scrollToAuth();\n     return;\n   }\n   const slot = minutes ?? 0;\n   const base = minutes === undefined ? nextHalfHour() : { day: startOfDay(day), minutes: slot };\n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx","patch":"Index: /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n+++ /workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx\n@@ -167,12 +167,16 @@\n   setAnchor(startOfDay(day));\n   setView(\"day\");\n };\n \n+const scrollToAuth = () => {\n+  document.getElementById(\"auth-panel\")?.scrollIntoView?.({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n+};\n+\n const openCreateForm = (day: Date, minutes?: number) => {\n   if (!session) {\n     setAuthTab(\"login\");\n-    document.getElementById(\"auth-panel\")?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: \"smooth\" });\n+    scrollToAuth();\n     return;\n   }\n   const slot = minutes ?? 0;\n   const base = minutes === undefined ? nextHalfHour() : { day: startOfDay(day), minutes: slot };\n","additions":5,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/App.tsx","time":{"start":1794352662693,"end":1794352662706}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c7c0c8a0001qvj6qlfyWCjQgm","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","messageID":"msg_1c7c096fb001KgO6XxNGMUw9xj"}}
