{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794352667668,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7c0dbf8001Z5vVak9khEZh70","messageID":"msg_1c7c0d0ea001VVI9dVeuzSX0b5","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352667668,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7c0dbfb001hDs4ILCs202Mjv","messageID":"msg_1c7c0d0ea001VVI9dVeuzSX0b5","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait, `scrollToAuth` is defined after its use in the JSX? In React, function declarations via `const` are not hoisted — but the usage is inside a callback (onClick handler), which executes later, after the component body has fully executed. So the const is initialized by then. Fine.\n\nBut `scrollToAuth` is defined in the component body before the JSX return → fine.\n\nLet me rebuild and rerun the test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794352667643,"end":1794352667663}}}
