{"type":"text","timestamp":1794352875641,"sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","part":{"id":"prt_1c7c40864001JshS947WOqJloc","messageID":"msg_1c7c3ea9b001PEE8jJcva36xqd","sessionID":"ses_e3847c4f2ffeRaGpXufKYD9yDm","type":"text","text":"<think>The gunicorn process was killed (by my pkill). The data dir still has the old db (the `rm -rf` didn't run because the shell was killed first, or it ran and then... no, events.db exists with an old timestamp 23:18 — the rm didn't happen).\n\nLet me restart the server carefully with `setsid` and nohup, and avoid pkill matching my own command line (use a pattern that doesn't match, e.g. `pkill -f \"gunicorn --bind\"`... that still appears in my command line. I'll use `pkill -f \"[g]unicorn\"` trick — the bracket prevents self-match).\n\nLet me restart the server.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794352875620,"end":1794352875636}}}
